Here is another pair. Well, as we can see here, the proximity rate is high but the gps close ratio is zero. That's because we missed the gps values during this period. When the sheep under the tree, the device cannot connect to the satellites and based on the power saving settings, if the device failed 4 times to connect the satellites, it will enter into sleep mode for 2 hours. 

Here is the evidence. During the period of 12 to 16, this pair has a very low gps valid ratio. That's because the N171 and N189 are put the collar on the side of the neck, while N182 just put the gps under the neck. When the sleep lie down, the gps will be blocked by the body and have a poor satellite signals. 

After removing the abnormal data, we can get a even higher correlation between the two series. 


